---
import SEO from '../components/SEO.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<!doctype html>

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<SEO
			title="Books | Fede Rodrigo"
			description="Books by Fede Rodrigo about technology leadership, business, incentives, institutions, and the systems that shape organizations"
			lang="en"
		/>
	</head>

	<body>
		<Header />

		<main>
			<section class="books-page-hero">
				<h1>Books</h1>

				<p class="lead">
					Practical ideas about technology leadership, business,
					incentives, and the systems that shape how people and
					organizations operate
				</p>

				<div class="page-statement">
					There Shouldn’t Be an “I” in CIO
				</div>
			</section>

			<section
				class="books-page-book books-page-book-featured"
				aria-labelledby="cio-book-title"
			>
				<div class="books-page-cover-wrapper">
					<a
						href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0F8MVPN4Q"
						target="_blank"
						rel="noopener noreferrer"
						class="books-page-cover-link"
						aria-label="View How to Become CIO and Succeed on Amazon"
					>
						<img
							src="/images/cio-book-cover.jpg"
							alt="Cover of How to Become CIO and Succeed"
							class="books-page-cover"
						/>
					</a>
				</div>

				<div class="books-page-content">
					<p class="books-page-label">
						Featured Book
					</p>

					<h2 id="cio-book-title">
						How to Become CIO and Succeed
					</h2>

					<p class="books-page-subtitle">
						People, Business, Strategy
					</p>

					<p>
						I wrote
						<strong>
							<em>How to Become CIO and Succeed</em>
						</strong>
						because it was the book I wish I had when I began my
						leadership journey.
					</p>

					<p>
						The CIO role is not about babysitting systems. It is about
						leading people, influencing the organization, shaping
						strategy, and driving the business forward.
					</p>

					<p>
						A transformative CIO does not simply manage technology.
						They build the right team, earn the trust of the business,
						and turn IT into a competitive advantage. When done
						right, Information Technology is not merely a cost
						center—it becomes a force multiplier.
					</p>

					<p>
						Drawing on more than 25 years of experience across
						enterprise applications, infrastructure, cybersecurity,
						M&A, and operational technology, the book explores what
						it takes to make IT a true business enabler.
					</p>

					<p>
						This is not a textbook or corporate fluff. It is a
						practical field guide for current and aspiring CIOs and
						IT leaders who want no-nonsense strategies,
						battle-tested insights, and practical leadership lessons.
					</p>

					<p>
						Success in leadership is not about calling the shots
						alone. It is about empowering people, fostering
						collaboration, and making IT a trusted business partner.
					</p>

					<div
						class="books-page-principles"
						aria-label="Leadership principles"
					>
						<span>People First</span>
						<span>Business Driven</span>
						<span>Technology Enabled</span>
					</div>

					<p class="books-page-closing">
						If you are here to maintain the status quo, turn back
						now.
					</p>

					<p class="books-page-action">
						<a
							href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0F8MVPN4Q"
							target="_blank"
							rel="noopener noreferrer"
						>
							View on Amazon →
						</a>
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section
				class="books-page-other"
				aria-labelledby="other-work-title"
			>
				<h2 id="other-work-title">
					Other Work
				</h2>

				<article
					class="books-page-book books-page-book-secondary"
					aria-labelledby="minimal-tolerance-title"
				>
					<div class="books-page-cover-wrapper">
						<a
							href="https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=5984574"
							target="_blank"
							rel="noopener noreferrer"
							class="books-page-cover-link"
							aria-label="Read The Minimal Tolerance Theorem on SSRN"
						>
							<img
								src="/images/book-cover.jpg"
								alt="Cover of A Theory of Minimal Tolerance"
								class="books-page-cover"
								loading="lazy"
							/>
						</a>
					</div>

					<div class="books-page-content">
						<p class="books-page-label">
							Forthcoming
						</p>

						<h3 id="minimal-tolerance-title">
							A Theory of Minimal Tolerance
						</h3>

						<p>
							A work exploring freedom, coercion, incentives,
							institutions, and the limits that should constrain
							political power.
						</p>

						<p>
							It develops a practical framework for examining the
							conditions under which state coercion may be morally
							tolerable, while recognizing that coercion never
							becomes morally legitimate.
						</p>

						<p class="books-page-action">
							<a
								href="https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=5984574"
								target="_blank"
								rel="noopener noreferrer"
							>
								Read The Minimal Tolerance Theorem on SSRN →
							</a>
						</p>
					</div>
				</article>
			</section>
		</main>

		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
